Vikram and Betal: The Fair Leader (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100136

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a village leader who was known for being fair,” said Betal. “He treated everyone equally.”

One day, two villagers came to him with a problem.

They both wanted to use the same piece of land.

The leader listened to both sides carefully.

Instead of choosing one person, he made a fair decision.

He said, “You will share the land and use it at different times.”

Both villagers agreed and were happy.

The village became peaceful again.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the leader special?”

Vikram replied, “His fairness and ability to think of everyone.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Fairness brings peace.
